WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:50.400


00:00:54.465 --> 00:00:55.199
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:55.999
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

00:00:55.999 --> 00:00:56.700
(This drama complied
with production guidelines...)

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.401
(for filming child actors and animals.)

00:01:15.329 --> 00:01:16.697
Do you want to go get some air?

00:01:17.264 --> 00:01:18.732
My morning's pretty open.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:22.236
On the phone you gave me,

00:01:24.338 --> 00:01:25.973
there aren't any numbers saved.

00:01:29.176 --> 00:01:30.611
It's completely empty.

00:01:31.545 --> 00:01:32.579
Just like me.

00:01:38.686 --> 00:01:41.322
Your old phone...

00:01:41.322 --> 00:01:43.490
and the bag with your wallet in it
are missing.

00:01:43.991 --> 00:01:44.858
You probably...

00:01:45.626 --> 00:01:48.762
lost them at the convenience store
where that little thief works.

00:01:49.897 --> 00:01:52.766
I already reported it, so they'll call.

00:01:57.538 --> 00:01:59.506
If I committed some kind of crime,

00:02:00.874 --> 00:02:02.810
just tell me. It's okay.

00:02:07.147 --> 00:02:09.883
You don't need to worry about
what those detectives said.

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:14.321
They were just leading you on
to get the answer they wanted and...

00:02:14.321 --> 00:02:15.122
No.

00:02:15.389 --> 00:02:17.057
When I was talking to the detectives,

00:02:17.524 --> 00:02:19.326
my heart was pounding so hard...

00:02:19.326 --> 00:02:20.661
that I wanted to run out of there.

00:02:21.695 --> 00:02:23.964
There has to be a reason I feel this way.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.134
Myo Jin.

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:30.004
Right now, the best thing
is for you to focus on treatment.

00:02:30.004 --> 00:02:31.538
And what exactly
does "the best thing" mean?

00:02:32.539 --> 00:02:33.841
You know...

00:02:33.841 --> 00:02:35.442
what happened to me, Jun Ho.

00:02:36.543 --> 00:02:38.078
You can see how frustrated I am.

00:02:38.078 --> 00:02:39.880
So why won't you just tell me everything?

00:02:46.253 --> 00:02:47.921
I talked it over with Dr. Jung.

00:02:48.522 --> 00:02:51.158
I asked whether it might help...

00:02:51.525 --> 00:02:54.395
if you tried, even little by little,

00:02:54.395 --> 00:02:56.096
to recall memories
connected to the accident.

00:02:56.096 --> 00:02:56.997
That's right.

00:02:57.765 --> 00:02:59.133
That's exactly what I think.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.101
But the answer was the opposite.

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:04.204
Talking about the accident...

00:03:05.572 --> 00:03:06.507
could actually...

00:03:07.074 --> 00:03:09.310
have a negative effect
on your state of mind.

00:03:09.944 --> 00:03:13.280
And that would only slow normal recovery.

00:03:13.547 --> 00:03:14.415
Really?

00:03:15.649 --> 00:03:17.484
So the reason
you can't tell me anything...

00:03:19.053 --> 00:03:20.554
is because it's all for my sake?

00:03:21.021 --> 00:03:22.156
Think carefully.

00:03:22.856 --> 00:03:24.792
You seem to be in danger right now.

00:03:25.326 --> 00:03:27.695
Instead of trying
to recover your memories,

00:03:27.695 --> 00:03:29.563
if you focus only on your emotions,

00:03:29.563 --> 00:03:32.032
things will only become
more complicated and confusing.

00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:34.134
That way of thinking is dangerous.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.136
Emotions...

00:03:36.136 --> 00:03:37.871
should be seen as a means to an end.

00:03:38.939 --> 00:03:40.240
A means to an end?

00:03:40.574 --> 00:03:43.243
When you're trying to recover your memory,
everything becomes a means to that end.

00:03:44.311 --> 00:03:47.915
Not just your own sensations,
feelings, and thoughts,

00:03:48.816 --> 00:03:50.250
but everything around you.

00:03:52.653 --> 00:03:54.622
How far...

00:03:54.622 --> 00:03:56.523
am I supposed to take that?

00:03:57.057 --> 00:03:59.827
That depends on how you choose to see it.

00:04:00.628 --> 00:04:02.196
Then that means...

00:04:03.831 --> 00:04:05.332
my fiancé...

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:07.735
would be included too, right?

00:04:08.335 --> 00:04:10.271
If that's how you see it, Ms. Ham.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.278
Thank you...

00:04:19.013 --> 00:04:20.581
for that advice...

00:04:21.348 --> 00:04:23.450
that I shouldn't trust anyone
until I get my memory back.

00:04:24.118 --> 00:04:27.288
Whether you trust someone or not
is your choice, Ms. Ham,

00:04:27.688 --> 00:04:29.323
but there's one thing you mustn't forget.

00:04:29.723 --> 00:04:30.691
What is it?

00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:32.927
If you don't trust someone,

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.196
that person won't trust you, either.

00:04:38.299 --> 00:04:39.300
That could become...

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:42.436
my biggest obstacle.

00:04:45.453 --> 00:04:48.222
(Distrust)

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.178
"H."

00:05:49.183 --> 00:05:50.184
Hee Su.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.454
Choi Hee Su.

00:06:04.999 --> 00:06:06.567
(Certificate of Resident Registration)

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:08.836
(Ryu Jun Ho, Ham Myo Jin)

00:06:14.876 --> 00:06:15.576
(Seoyeon-dong Community Service Center)

00:06:15.576 --> 00:06:18.579
Please insert your card
into the slot in the correct direction.

00:06:27.488 --> 00:06:29.724
"263, Gahan-ro."

00:06:38.766 --> 00:06:39.533
It's a gift.

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:41.135
(National Forensic Service)

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:46.474
At the Jebudo Island villa,

00:06:47.041 --> 00:06:48.910
they found the weapon used in the crime.

00:06:49.677 --> 00:06:50.545
A weapon?

00:06:51.746 --> 00:06:52.647
A crime?

00:06:53.447 --> 00:06:56.117
Our whole direction in the investigation
has been completely wrong.

00:06:57.752 --> 00:06:59.520
I looked over
the initial autopsy results again,

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:00.855
and both of the deceased...

00:07:01.055 --> 00:07:02.924
were listed as having died in the fire.

00:07:04.926 --> 00:07:07.662
It's been long since the accident,
and only now...

00:07:08.362 --> 00:07:09.764
Did you ever imagine...

00:07:11.232 --> 00:07:13.701
someone could commit murder
in that blazing inferno?

00:07:30.618 --> 00:07:32.954
I'm Ryu Jun Ho. I work in architecture.

00:07:34.188 --> 00:07:35.823
I'm sorry for coming here so abruptly.

00:08:03.284 --> 00:08:04.752
Only a few people at the top...

00:08:04.752 --> 00:08:07.088
know that I'm serving as a judge,

00:08:08.422 --> 00:08:10.191
so I suppose someone has a loose tongue.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:13.661
If you knew about me in advance,

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:18.299
then you must also be aware
of the qualifications to be announced.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.570
Applicants must hold
a Korean architect's license...

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:25.239
and have at least ten years...

00:08:25.239 --> 00:08:27.008
of practical experience
in architectural design.

00:08:27.008 --> 00:08:27.875
However,

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.712
I don't meet that requirement.

00:08:32.446 --> 00:08:33.714
This is a project...

00:08:33.714 --> 00:08:35.917
to build the largest museum in Asia.

00:08:37.184 --> 00:08:39.487
The project seems far too large...

00:08:39.487 --> 00:08:41.289
to take on with ambition alone.

00:08:42.156 --> 00:08:43.190
Of course,

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:45.426
I understand why you'd think that.

00:08:45.426 --> 00:08:46.727
As you know,

00:08:48.563 --> 00:08:52.667
most of the great architects
since the 20th century...

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:56.070
only produced their signature works
after turning 40.

00:08:57.405 --> 00:08:59.106
There will still be...

00:09:00.441 --> 00:09:01.442
many opportunities ahead.

00:09:01.809 --> 00:09:04.045
If you would give me that opportunity,

00:09:04.045 --> 00:09:04.879
I'm confident...

00:09:06.314 --> 00:09:07.949
I can surprise you, sir.

00:09:11.285 --> 00:09:13.621
I will bring you a design for this museum.

00:09:14.789 --> 00:09:17.692
And if there's even
the slightest resemblance...

00:09:17.692 --> 00:09:20.528
to any museum you've ever seen
or can remember,

00:09:20.528 --> 00:09:21.996
I'll withdraw that very moment.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.298
I'm sure everyone else
is preparing with that same resolve.

00:09:24.298 --> 00:09:25.533
At the official judging,

00:09:25.533 --> 00:09:27.235
I'll submit a different design.

00:09:27.235 --> 00:09:28.536
Likewise,

00:09:28.536 --> 00:09:31.138
if it isn't a museum
you've truly never seen before,

00:09:32.406 --> 00:09:34.008
please eliminate me on the spot.

00:09:34.408 --> 00:09:36.978
I suggest you think very carefully.

00:09:36.978 --> 00:09:37.879
you still seem too young for this.

00:09:37.879 --> 00:09:40.915
Even the world-renowned architects
you mentioned...

00:09:41.549 --> 00:09:42.516
must have had a time,

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:44.619
like me now,

00:09:44.619 --> 00:09:46.654
when they struggled to prove themselves.

00:09:46.654 --> 00:09:47.622
And...

00:09:47.989 --> 00:09:50.191
there must have been one person
who recognized that effort.

00:09:50.191 --> 00:09:51.192
Right now,

00:09:52.827 --> 00:09:54.328
I desperately need that one person too.

00:10:01.836 --> 00:10:03.004
Mr. Ryu.

00:10:04.438 --> 00:10:05.273
Yes?

00:10:06.707 --> 00:10:07.942
What's the name of your firm?

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:11.212
Mono Architecture.

00:10:11.846 --> 00:10:12.680
Mono?

00:10:14.248 --> 00:10:15.550
The Mono I know?

00:10:37.104 --> 00:10:37.939
Myo Jin.

00:10:38.272 --> 00:10:39.340
It's been such a long time.

00:10:41.742 --> 00:10:44.278
Yeah, it's been a while.

00:10:45.112 --> 00:10:47.615
You two seriously hurt me.

00:10:47.615 --> 00:10:49.850
How could you both
cut off contact at the same time?

00:10:50.284 --> 00:10:51.252
I'm honestly offended.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.654
Actually,

00:10:53.654 --> 00:10:55.990
I was sick for a while.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.491
So I was taking some time off.

00:10:57.491 --> 00:10:58.793
Really?

00:10:59.694 --> 00:11:01.262
Then what about the rich lady?

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:05.032
You mean Hee Su, right?

00:11:05.032 --> 00:11:06.300
Of course.

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:07.868
Who else would I mean besides you two?

00:11:09.537 --> 00:11:10.404
Well,

00:11:11.505 --> 00:11:13.641
Hee Su wasn't feeling well either,
so she was hospitalized.

00:11:13.641 --> 00:11:14.742
Seriously?

00:11:15.009 --> 00:11:16.410
You two were that close,

00:11:16.978 --> 00:11:18.479
and even got sick at the same time.

00:11:21.883 --> 00:11:24.485
So I guess
you'll be alone at the studio for a while.

00:11:25.319 --> 00:11:26.220
The studio?

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:27.221
Yeah.

00:11:27.221 --> 00:11:29.557
You two painted together
at the studio every day.

00:11:29.957 --> 00:11:31.325
Aren't you headed there even now?

00:11:42.236 --> 00:11:44.038
Your fingerprint is registered here.

00:11:44.038 --> 00:11:45.773
How could you forget this place?

00:11:46.007 --> 00:11:47.875
I was just confused for a second.

00:11:47.875 --> 00:11:49.176
I remember now.

00:11:50.344 --> 00:11:51.779
Okay.

00:11:57.318 --> 00:11:58.619
I've never seen this painting before.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:00.888
You're the one on the right, right?

00:12:05.359 --> 00:12:07.094
Since it says "H,"

00:12:07.728 --> 00:12:09.697
the rich lady painted it.

00:12:16.604 --> 00:12:18.339
I should get going.

00:12:18.606 --> 00:12:19.640
You'll come again, right?

00:12:20.641 --> 00:12:23.878
After you're done,
do you have time to talk to me?

00:12:23.878 --> 00:12:25.012
Time?

00:12:25.012 --> 00:12:25.913
Why?

00:12:27.114 --> 00:12:30.218
I wanted to ask you about Hee Su.

00:12:30.218 --> 00:12:31.919
Ask me?

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.055
You were the one closest to her,

00:12:34.055 --> 00:12:35.656
so what could you possibly want to ask me?

00:12:37.592 --> 00:12:39.560
I really have to go.

00:12:40.861 --> 00:12:41.929
Okay.

00:12:43.197 --> 00:12:44.098
But...

00:12:44.599 --> 00:12:46.534
this painting is really good.

00:12:46.801 --> 00:12:48.469
You two are really talented.

00:13:00.748 --> 00:13:03.251
You didn't come because you missed me,

00:13:19.033 --> 00:13:19.867
so why?

00:13:20.201 --> 00:13:22.069
Did something come up
that you want to ask me?

00:13:24.272 --> 00:13:26.641
That's right, I remember.

00:13:28.943 --> 00:13:29.844
Hee Su.

00:13:32.914 --> 00:13:34.715
We were definitely together.

00:13:41.022 --> 00:13:42.356
Come on.

00:13:47.261 --> 00:13:49.230
Hey, isn't it ridiculous?

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.599
Nobody knows about this place.

00:13:52.567 --> 00:13:53.501
No way.

00:13:53.834 --> 00:13:55.736
It's this nice,
so why doesn't anyone know?

00:13:56.337 --> 00:13:59.073
Are you secretly
keeping people from coming here?

00:14:00.775 --> 00:14:02.310
Honestly, I wish I were.

00:14:03.377 --> 00:14:04.679
Is there some way?

00:14:05.713 --> 00:14:07.481
You could ask your dad...

00:14:07.481 --> 00:14:10.117
to build another villa here.

00:14:10.384 --> 00:14:12.987
Then this whole area would
basically become your own private beach.

00:14:13.854 --> 00:14:16.224
Ham Myo Jin.

00:14:17.091 --> 00:14:18.326
You're a genius.

00:14:19.393 --> 00:14:21.295
My dad would totally do that much.

00:14:21.562 --> 00:14:22.530
Seriously?

00:14:22.897 --> 00:14:24.031
Of course.

00:14:24.365 --> 00:14:25.366
Hey.

00:14:25.366 --> 00:14:27.602
Are you saying that
knowing what kind of person my dad is?

00:14:28.769 --> 00:14:32.039
You sound like you know
exactly what he's like.

00:14:33.341 --> 00:14:34.842
I was kidding.

00:14:35.576 --> 00:14:36.844
Don't say this to him.

00:14:36.844 --> 00:14:38.412
He'll think I'm weird.

00:14:42.316 --> 00:14:44.652
Wait.
He probably still doesn't know who I am.

00:14:45.553 --> 00:14:46.487
He does.

00:14:47.521 --> 00:14:48.823
I've already told him about you.

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:50.458
He says he wants to meet you too.

00:14:51.359 --> 00:14:52.193
Really?

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:53.227
Yeah.

00:14:53.227 --> 00:14:55.696
He said once he's back,
we should all go on vacation together.

00:14:56.497 --> 00:14:57.932
That sounds fun.

00:14:57.932 --> 00:14:59.033
I could introduce myself to him.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:01.135
But who knows.

00:15:01.535 --> 00:15:04.238
His schedule is all over the place.

00:15:05.039 --> 00:15:07.375
So you have no idea when he'll be back?

00:15:07.942 --> 00:15:10.845
Yeah. Sometimes he just suddenly shows up.

00:15:12.246 --> 00:15:14.749
And he still hasn't said
when he's coming back?

00:15:15.049 --> 00:15:15.917
Hey.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:17.818
Why are you so curious...

00:15:17.818 --> 00:15:19.120
about when my dad's coming back?

00:15:20.121 --> 00:15:21.889
You ask every chance you get.

00:15:23.558 --> 00:15:24.792
It's just...

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:32.500
Let's not make a good relationship
awkward for no reason.

00:15:33.401 --> 00:15:35.403
I want to stay your friend.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.206
I don't want to become family.

00:15:39.874 --> 00:15:40.875
What are you even saying?

00:15:42.143 --> 00:15:43.611
Though that would be kind of funny too.

00:15:44.545 --> 00:15:46.681
You giving birth to my younger sibling.

00:15:48.149 --> 00:15:49.717
Then I can call you "Mom," right?

00:15:51.085 --> 00:15:51.919
Hey!

00:15:52.253 --> 00:15:53.921
Mom!

00:15:54.255 --> 00:15:55.856
Get over here!

00:15:55.856 --> 00:15:58.559
Mom, I want a little brother.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.294
Mom.

00:16:14.709 --> 00:16:16.944
Your old phone...

00:16:16.944 --> 00:16:18.980
and the bag with your wallet in it
are missing.

00:16:19.614 --> 00:16:20.615
You probably...

00:16:21.148 --> 00:16:24.252
lost them at the convenience store
where that little thief works.

00:16:33.928 --> 00:16:34.862
Hey.

00:16:34.862 --> 00:16:35.930
Hey.

00:16:36.964 --> 00:16:38.199
That woman came again.

00:16:43.137 --> 00:16:44.472
We should talk for a minute.

00:17:01.856 --> 00:17:02.857
How'd you know...

00:17:03.724 --> 00:17:04.725
I took it?

00:17:05.059 --> 00:17:06.661
If you hadn't listened again today,

00:17:06.661 --> 00:17:08.095
you would've ended up
at the police station again.

00:17:08.462 --> 00:17:09.397
Whatever.

00:17:11.432 --> 00:17:12.667
But is that rumor true?

00:17:13.834 --> 00:17:14.869
About the murder?

00:17:17.071 --> 00:17:18.172
Be honest with me.

00:17:19.507 --> 00:17:21.209
Who exactly are they saying I killed?

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:23.511
What are you talking about?

00:17:24.378 --> 00:17:25.513
I mean that guy.

00:17:25.513 --> 00:17:27.381
The one who tried to hit me
at the police station.

00:17:28.182 --> 00:17:29.050
What?

00:17:31.319 --> 00:17:32.687
Jun Ho?

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.855
You saw my mom causing a scene
at the police station, right?

00:17:36.824 --> 00:17:38.426
They say that guy is seriously scary.

00:17:40.328 --> 00:17:41.295
No way.

00:17:41.662 --> 00:17:44.065
Didn't the chairman
of the company he works for die recently?

00:17:45.733 --> 00:17:47.702
He burned to death in his sleep
when the villa exploded.

00:17:49.103 --> 00:17:50.304
And wasn't that chairman super rich?

00:17:52.573 --> 00:17:53.841
If he had nothing to do
with that accident,

00:17:53.841 --> 00:17:55.343
why would the police
show up at his house...

00:17:56.143 --> 00:17:57.445
again and again?

00:17:57.445 --> 00:17:58.746
You know...

00:17:58.746 --> 00:18:00.414
what happened to me, Jun Ho.

00:18:00.648 --> 00:18:02.083
You can see how frustrated I am,

00:18:02.083 --> 00:18:03.885
so why won't you just tell me everything?

00:18:04.418 --> 00:18:07.221
Right now, the best thing
is for you to focus on treatment.

00:18:07.221 --> 00:18:08.923
This is a time to be careful.

00:18:09.924 --> 00:18:10.858
Don't...

00:18:11.759 --> 00:18:13.194
overinterpret everything.

00:18:13.861 --> 00:18:15.630
Do you think locking your door
will stop rumors from spreading?

00:18:16.097 --> 00:18:18.232
What, do you think
everyone around here is stupid?

00:18:18.733 --> 00:18:21.335
I heard you got in a car accident
back then and hit your head.

00:18:22.937 --> 00:18:24.539
That's why you were
in the hospital all this time.

00:18:27.074 --> 00:18:30.077
So people are talking about me too?

00:18:30.411 --> 00:18:31.312
Are you some attention seeker?

00:18:33.214 --> 00:18:35.816
Why would anyone care
about someone who doesn't even live here?

00:18:36.083 --> 00:18:37.451
I don't live here?

00:18:37.451 --> 00:18:38.920
That's enough.

00:18:39.287 --> 00:18:41.722
If you're that curious,
go ask at the police station.

00:18:48.996 --> 00:18:49.964
Where's my phone?

00:18:50.264 --> 00:18:51.132
What phone?

00:18:53.234 --> 00:18:54.335
That's all there is.

00:18:55.469 --> 00:18:56.404
Give it.

00:19:43.417 --> 00:19:44.285
Mono?

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:47.154
The Mono I know?

00:19:47.355 --> 00:19:48.456
Yes, that's right.

00:19:50.925 --> 00:19:53.027
Chairman Choi Young Ho
mentioned you to me a few times,

00:19:53.027 --> 00:19:54.929
but I never expected
to see you here like this.

00:19:55.329 --> 00:19:56.197
Excuse me?

00:19:56.397 --> 00:19:58.499
People had all sorts of things to say,

00:19:58.499 --> 00:20:00.635
but he had exceptional instincts.

00:20:01.836 --> 00:20:04.939
Bringing renowned foreign designers
onto an advisory board...

00:20:05.706 --> 00:20:08.242
and having them involved
from the earliest design stage...

00:20:08.242 --> 00:20:10.678
was first introduced in Korea
by Chairman Choi.

00:20:11.078 --> 00:20:13.381
I was overseas
when I heard about the accident,

00:20:14.248 --> 00:20:15.883
so I wasn't able
to pay my respects properly.

00:20:18.319 --> 00:20:19.320
I'm sorry.

00:20:19.854 --> 00:20:23.624
I had no idea...

00:20:23.624 --> 00:20:25.059
Chairman Choi and you knew each other.

00:20:25.059 --> 00:20:26.127
If I had known,

00:20:27.495 --> 00:20:29.430
I never would've come here like this.

00:20:29.897 --> 00:20:32.600
Please pretend today never happened.

00:20:34.702 --> 00:20:35.570
Mr. Ryu.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:37.104
Yes?

00:20:37.838 --> 00:20:39.941
Do I strike you as someone
who's swayed by what others say?

00:20:42.577 --> 00:20:45.513
I've never done anything
that didn't move my heart.

00:20:46.414 --> 00:20:48.216
And that's still true now.

00:20:48.616 --> 00:20:50.284
I've always wondered...

00:20:50.284 --> 00:20:53.020
what kind of person you were...

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:54.422
for Chairman Choi to praise you so highly.

00:20:55.323 --> 00:20:57.291
What you showed me here today...

00:20:57.291 --> 00:21:00.061
has only made me more curious.

00:21:00.728 --> 00:21:03.297
What the late chairman said...

00:21:04.131 --> 00:21:06.200
and the judgment I'm making now...

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.268
are two different things.

00:21:10.304 --> 00:21:12.907
Let me see your work, Mr. Ryu.

00:21:14.709 --> 00:21:15.977
Come to my studio.

00:21:30.725 --> 00:21:31.826
You're here.

00:21:33.895 --> 00:21:35.263
There's something I want to know.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:37.031
Yeah?

00:21:37.632 --> 00:21:38.466
What?

00:21:41.636 --> 00:21:42.870
I want to know who she is.

00:21:50.411 --> 00:21:51.279
Her?

00:21:51.812 --> 00:21:53.047
She's your friend.

00:21:54.348 --> 00:21:55.349
What kind of friend?

00:21:56.350 --> 00:21:57.518
What do you mean, what kind?

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:02.490
Just the kind of ordinary friend
anyone might have.

00:22:03.057 --> 00:22:04.825
Her name is Hee Su, right?

00:22:06.027 --> 00:22:06.961
I'm not sure.

00:22:07.795 --> 00:22:10.364
I don't think she was
that important a friend.

00:22:11.499 --> 00:22:12.500
Really?

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:17.438
Can we talk later?

00:22:17.438 --> 00:22:19.473
I need to wrap this up and head out.

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:23.811
Get some rest.

00:22:23.811 --> 00:22:24.845
You look tired.

00:22:31.052 --> 00:22:32.053
So...

00:22:33.821 --> 00:22:35.723
you really don't know this woman?

00:22:39.327 --> 00:22:40.228
Why?

00:22:40.695 --> 00:22:43.798
Is she on your mind that much?

00:22:47.568 --> 00:22:48.469
No.

00:22:49.470 --> 00:22:51.038
Like you said, Jun Ho,

00:22:51.038 --> 00:22:52.773
I hope we weren't that close either.

00:23:14.395 --> 00:23:17.398
(Special Sale, Bread, Buy 1 Get 1)

00:23:57.138 --> 00:23:58.072
Hey.

00:23:59.507 --> 00:24:00.575
Sorry.

00:24:03.678 --> 00:24:07.048
But I'm hungry.

00:24:20.027 --> 00:24:20.995
Eat this.

00:24:22.330 --> 00:24:23.764
Thank you.

00:24:33.507 --> 00:24:34.976
Thank you.

00:24:48.256 --> 00:24:49.457
I know.

00:24:49.457 --> 00:24:51.926
I know what a good man you are.

00:24:52.426 --> 00:24:54.328
I know that better than anyone.

00:24:55.463 --> 00:24:57.665
But what does that get you?

00:24:57.665 --> 00:24:59.033
Does anybody give you
some kind of medal for it?

00:25:10.678 --> 00:25:12.380
Do you think that woman
is going to leave you alone...

00:25:13.247 --> 00:25:15.049
when you know
every single thing there is to know?

00:25:16.450 --> 00:25:18.085
What, are you going to regret it...

00:25:18.085 --> 00:25:19.787
only after someone
puts a knife through your neck?

00:25:20.087 --> 00:25:22.490
They're not the kind of people
to let this end here.

00:25:50.318 --> 00:25:51.152
Myo Jin.

00:25:55.790 --> 00:25:56.591
Jun Ho?

00:26:08.603 --> 00:26:09.770
- I'm sorry.
- What?

00:26:09.770 --> 00:26:12.373
Work had me way too on edge earlier.

00:26:13.107 --> 00:26:15.543
I couldn't even give you a proper answer.

00:26:17.879 --> 00:26:20.014
Did you come back just to tell me that?

00:26:23.351 --> 00:26:25.152
They're monsters in human skin.

00:26:26.020 --> 00:26:28.489
If you keep dragging your feet,
someone's going to bleed again.

00:26:29.857 --> 00:26:32.093
If you don't want to end up
in real trouble,

00:26:32.093 --> 00:26:34.695
you need to move right now
before it comes back on you.

00:26:36.530 --> 00:26:38.699
Just trust me and follow my lead.

00:26:39.200 --> 00:26:41.402
You've never lost out
by listening to me before, have you?

00:26:56.217 --> 00:26:57.084
So?

00:27:00.922 --> 00:27:01.923
Hey.

00:27:05.793 --> 00:27:08.162
What's this plan of yours?

00:27:11.198 --> 00:27:13.401
What could be so important...

00:27:13.401 --> 00:27:15.136
that we can't even be together
this late at night?

00:27:15.903 --> 00:27:16.737
Right?

00:27:17.338 --> 00:27:18.573
Don't do that anymore.

00:27:19.340 --> 00:27:21.943
Even if something's bothering me,
we can talk about it later.

00:27:22.310 --> 00:27:23.177
Okay.

00:27:23.978 --> 00:27:24.812
I'm sorry.

00:27:26.914 --> 00:27:28.950
But aren't you late?

00:27:28.950 --> 00:27:30.351
No, it's okay.

00:27:30.351 --> 00:27:31.953
I pushed it back a little.

00:27:32.286 --> 00:27:33.221
I won't be late.

00:27:37.124 --> 00:27:38.326
About what you asked earlier,

00:27:39.293 --> 00:27:40.695
something came back to me.

00:27:41.762 --> 00:27:42.597
What?

00:27:43.130 --> 00:27:44.599
That friend, Choi Hee Su.

00:27:47.168 --> 00:27:48.102
I feel like...

00:27:49.003 --> 00:27:52.240
there were times
she was kind of rough with you.

00:27:53.207 --> 00:27:55.042
So I don't think I saw her after that.

00:27:57.245 --> 00:27:59.013
What happened?

00:28:01.582 --> 00:28:03.851
I don't remember clearly,

00:28:05.553 --> 00:28:07.255
but maybe I should say
she was harsh with her words.

00:28:12.059 --> 00:28:14.528
I don't remember...

00:28:15.296 --> 00:28:16.764
anything like that at all.

00:28:18.900 --> 00:28:19.967
But Myo Jin.

00:28:21.869 --> 00:28:22.703
Yes?

00:28:23.938 --> 00:28:26.541
What made you think
of that friend, Hee Su?

00:28:28.276 --> 00:28:30.044
And where did that photo come from?

00:28:33.314 --> 00:28:35.182
I ran into a friend at the hospital.

00:28:36.017 --> 00:28:36.918
A friend?

00:28:37.718 --> 00:28:38.586
Yes.

00:28:39.453 --> 00:28:41.722
We only asked how each other was doing,
and then went our separate ways,

00:28:41.722 --> 00:28:43.190
so we didn't talk long.

00:28:44.125 --> 00:28:46.694
I see.
I guess you all knew each other well.

00:28:48.496 --> 00:28:49.664
I guess so.

00:28:51.899 --> 00:28:53.100
Did you get their contact information?

00:28:54.535 --> 00:28:56.137
Invite them over sometime.

00:28:58.806 --> 00:29:01.008
I gave my number.

00:29:03.878 --> 00:29:05.046
I'd like to meet that friend too...

00:29:05.947 --> 00:29:07.048
and see what kind of person they are.

00:29:09.684 --> 00:29:11.219
I'll say you said that if I get a call.

00:29:12.620 --> 00:29:13.454
Okay.

00:29:16.490 --> 00:29:18.459
I should get going now.

00:29:35.376 --> 00:29:36.577
I want to know who she is.

00:29:37.778 --> 00:29:38.679
So...

00:29:40.481 --> 00:29:42.316
you really don't know this woman?

00:30:18.920 --> 00:30:22.456
(No Entry - Under Investigation)

00:30:55.389 --> 00:30:56.958
This villa's burned to the ground.

00:30:57.792 --> 00:30:58.960
What brings you here?

00:31:01.229 --> 00:31:02.296
Hello.

00:31:02.663 --> 00:31:03.864
It looks like you're from Seoul.

00:31:04.498 --> 00:31:05.733
What brings you all the way out here?

00:31:09.170 --> 00:31:10.338
I'm sorry,

00:31:10.771 --> 00:31:12.673
but it's been a while
since I've been here,

00:31:12.974 --> 00:31:14.775
so I was wondering
if you happen to know me.

00:31:16.277 --> 00:31:18.012
I'm the village chief.

00:31:18.379 --> 00:31:21.015
This villa belongs to
the chairman's daughter.

00:31:21.883 --> 00:31:22.884
The chairman?

00:31:23.851 --> 00:31:25.987
You don't know
Chairman Choi of Mono Group?

00:31:26.254 --> 00:31:27.922
Don't you watch the news?

00:31:28.189 --> 00:31:29.924
That explosion happened at the villa,

00:31:29.924 --> 00:31:32.293
and it caused a stir.

00:31:32.293 --> 00:31:34.095
The chairman and his daughter both died.

00:31:36.097 --> 00:31:38.466
Do you know this woman by any chance?

00:31:39.667 --> 00:31:40.902
That's Ms. Choi,

00:31:41.869 --> 00:31:43.905
and the woman next to her is you.

00:31:45.640 --> 00:31:47.608
Do you know Hee Su well?

00:31:47.942 --> 00:31:49.744
No, not really.

00:31:50.478 --> 00:31:53.548
You should try that restaurant over there.

00:31:53.881 --> 00:31:56.350
The owner manages the villa too,

00:31:56.350 --> 00:31:57.585
and whenever Ms. Choi came,

00:31:57.585 --> 00:31:59.253
she'd bring meals up and all that.

00:32:01.022 --> 00:32:02.490
Okay.

00:32:04.392 --> 00:32:05.693
Poor them.

00:32:06.727 --> 00:32:08.696
That was taken
the last time you all came to visit.

00:32:08.696 --> 00:32:10.264
You all came in to eat together.

00:32:10.698 --> 00:32:13.200
Were there only three of us at the villa?

00:32:13.434 --> 00:32:14.802
Back then, yeah.

00:32:14.802 --> 00:32:16.637
And not long ago, you came by yourself.

00:32:17.071 --> 00:32:18.072
By myself?

00:32:18.072 --> 00:32:18.940
Yeah.

00:32:19.373 --> 00:32:21.242
You came to see Ms. Choi,

00:32:21.242 --> 00:32:22.443
but I told you she was out,

00:32:22.443 --> 00:32:24.045
and that you should wait here.

00:32:24.946 --> 00:32:25.813
Right.

00:32:25.813 --> 00:32:27.415
That's when you left your phone behind.

00:32:27.415 --> 00:32:28.249
Hold on.

00:32:28.416 --> 00:32:29.350
My phone?

00:32:29.350 --> 00:32:31.285
Yeah. Once you saw Ms. Choi coming back,

00:32:31.285 --> 00:32:32.887
you rushed out.

00:32:33.187 --> 00:32:35.089
Later, I saw you'd left your phone behind.

00:32:35.489 --> 00:32:37.291
I thought you'd come back for it
right away.

00:32:37.291 --> 00:32:38.059
Here it is.

00:32:39.627 --> 00:32:41.195
Then your accident happened
out of nowhere,

00:32:41.195 --> 00:32:42.930
and it completely slipped my mind.

00:32:45.766 --> 00:32:47.368
It's finally back with its owner.

00:32:48.736 --> 00:32:49.770
It doesn't work, does it?

00:32:50.171 --> 00:32:51.973
I turned it on a few times
to try and find you,

00:32:51.973 --> 00:32:53.007
but it didn't work.

00:32:53.741 --> 00:32:54.709
I see.

00:32:54.709 --> 00:32:56.611
Before it stopped working,

00:32:56.611 --> 00:32:58.779
there was one call from Seoul.

00:32:58.779 --> 00:33:00.948
They said it was important
and that you absolutely had to call back.

00:33:01.582 --> 00:33:03.484
Hold on, let me find the number.

00:33:03.484 --> 00:33:04.318
I put it right...

00:33:04.318 --> 00:33:05.486
Here it is.

00:33:06.721 --> 00:33:07.555
Here.

00:33:08.923 --> 00:33:11.158
(September)

00:33:31.979 --> 00:33:34.782
May I ask where this is?

00:33:35.316 --> 00:33:36.217
Here?

00:33:36.584 --> 00:33:37.585
It's a repair shop.

00:33:38.152 --> 00:33:39.086
Jigu Electronics.

00:33:40.121 --> 00:33:41.188
A repair shop?

00:33:44.225 --> 00:33:46.260
(Jigu Electronics)

00:33:46.661 --> 00:33:47.628
Goodness.

00:33:47.628 --> 00:33:50.731
I told you I'm not the type
to just run my mouth first.

00:33:50.731 --> 00:33:52.400
I'm a careful man.

00:33:52.400 --> 00:33:53.534
Deeply careful.

00:33:53.534 --> 00:33:55.670
Please don't make deep jokes like that.

00:33:55.670 --> 00:33:59.207
You definitely said
this laptop could be fixed.

00:33:59.207 --> 00:34:00.808
You said you'd make it...

00:34:00.808 --> 00:34:02.577
even more powerful
than those ONVIDIA graphics cards.

00:34:02.577 --> 00:34:03.811
But what is this?

00:34:03.811 --> 00:34:06.747
It's even glitchier now
than it was before the repair.

00:34:07.181 --> 00:34:08.115
I mean,

00:34:08.115 --> 00:34:09.450
the second I logged into the game,

00:34:09.450 --> 00:34:11.285
I just died right away.

00:34:11.285 --> 00:34:12.386
Bang, dead.

00:34:12.386 --> 00:34:14.589
Bang, dead.

00:34:14.589 --> 00:34:16.857
Of course, you're going to die.

00:34:16.857 --> 00:34:19.560
The graphics aren't the problem.

00:34:19.560 --> 00:34:21.062
When avatars start shooting each other,

00:34:21.062 --> 00:34:22.296
you're going to get shot too, right?

00:34:22.296 --> 00:34:23.431
How are you not supposed to get hit?

00:34:23.431 --> 00:34:25.533
You get shot, the zone closes in,
you run into enemies,

00:34:25.533 --> 00:34:26.534
and then once your energy runs out,

00:34:26.534 --> 00:34:28.269
you're out. Simple as that.

00:34:28.269 --> 00:34:31.973
That's why I told you
to find recovery items no matter what.

00:34:31.973 --> 00:34:34.508
Recovery items?

00:34:34.508 --> 00:34:36.344
You mean, like an energy drink?

00:34:36.344 --> 00:34:39.881
Energy drinks only restore 40 boost.

00:34:39.881 --> 00:34:40.715
What's the point of that?

00:34:40.715 --> 00:34:42.516
You stack a med kit on top of it,

00:34:42.516 --> 00:34:44.518
and then you shoot right up to 80.

00:34:44.886 --> 00:34:46.754
First, go buy those two items
and try again.

00:34:46.754 --> 00:34:47.989
And if you still die fast,

00:34:47.989 --> 00:34:50.291
then I'll personally teach you...

00:34:50.558 --> 00:34:52.293
the ultimate avatar strategy, okay?

00:34:53.794 --> 00:34:55.429
Okay. For real this time?

00:34:55.763 --> 00:34:56.831
Why can't you trust me?

00:34:56.831 --> 00:34:58.232
Go on, now. I'm busy.

00:34:58.966 --> 00:35:00.234
What was I supposed to do again?

00:35:00.668 --> 00:35:01.769
Sir.

00:35:02.470 --> 00:35:03.604
Promise to tell me the strategy.

00:35:03.604 --> 00:35:04.805
I promise.

00:35:04.805 --> 00:35:06.574
- There, stamped.
- Now get out of here.

00:35:06.574 --> 00:35:07.508
All right, I'm going.

00:35:10.545 --> 00:35:11.546
Hello.

00:35:12.113 --> 00:35:14.282
I was told you called my phone.

00:35:15.616 --> 00:35:17.285
What was it that you left here
to be repaired?

00:35:17.285 --> 00:35:18.886
Everything but batteries can be fixed.

00:35:18.886 --> 00:35:20.288
You'd have to buy a new battery,
that's why.

00:35:21.222 --> 00:35:22.390
It's just that...

00:35:22.390 --> 00:35:24.492
I can't really remember what I brought in.

00:35:24.492 --> 00:35:25.660
What are you talking about?

00:35:25.660 --> 00:35:27.028
How can you not remember
what you brought in?

00:35:28.362 --> 00:35:29.196
Wait.

00:35:30.197 --> 00:35:32.567
Myo...

00:35:32.567 --> 00:35:33.834
Ham Myo Jin.

00:35:33.834 --> 00:35:34.835
Do you know me?

00:35:34.835 --> 00:35:35.836
Of course, I do.

00:35:36.304 --> 00:35:38.773
But I heard you had a serious accident.

00:35:39.740 --> 00:35:40.942
Yes.

00:35:40.942 --> 00:35:43.344
I still can't remember things very well.

00:35:44.312 --> 00:35:45.479
You can't remember?

00:35:46.113 --> 00:35:47.281
That's bad.

00:35:47.281 --> 00:35:49.317
There's still quite a bit left for me
to collect on the balance.

00:35:50.084 --> 00:35:51.118
The balance?

00:35:51.852 --> 00:35:52.820
Money?

00:35:52.820 --> 00:35:53.955
What do I do now?

00:35:55.723 --> 00:35:58.025
Anyway, just come with me.

00:35:58.025 --> 00:35:59.026
Come on in.

00:35:59.894 --> 00:36:01.262
This really isn't good.

00:36:04.665 --> 00:36:05.800
Take a seat.

00:36:09.170 --> 00:36:10.137
But somehow,

00:36:10.805 --> 00:36:12.139
your whole vibe feels different.

00:36:12.874 --> 00:36:14.041
Maybe because it's been a while.

00:36:14.342 --> 00:36:15.142
Sorry?

00:36:15.142 --> 00:36:16.110
How do I put it?

00:36:16.110 --> 00:36:19.213
You've got this peaceful kind of vibe now,

00:36:19.213 --> 00:36:20.481
but also flex.

00:36:20.481 --> 00:36:21.449
No.

00:36:21.716 --> 00:36:24.051
Graceful, but elegant too.

00:36:24.051 --> 00:36:25.319
What was it I brought in?

00:36:26.120 --> 00:36:26.954
Wait.

00:36:29.991 --> 00:36:31.092
(Lee Sang Ho - National Police Agency)

00:36:38.733 --> 00:36:39.934
You didn't ask for a repair.

00:36:39.934 --> 00:36:41.035
You asked to look into a person.

00:36:41.736 --> 00:36:44.038
But are you sure you're okay?
You said you're still not yourself.

00:36:44.038 --> 00:36:46.073
It's fine. Just tell me.

00:36:46.607 --> 00:36:47.475
Okay.

00:36:47.475 --> 00:36:50.611
The pictures might be
a little hard to look at,

00:36:50.978 --> 00:36:52.046
but just take a look first.

00:36:52.780 --> 00:36:53.614
Here.

00:36:54.282 --> 00:36:55.349
This man here...

00:36:55.349 --> 00:36:56.884
is the one you hired me to investigate.

00:36:56.884 --> 00:36:58.819
He runs around with gangsters,

00:36:58.819 --> 00:37:01.122
does loan-sharking, violence,
and even dirty-fixer work.

00:37:01.122 --> 00:37:03.691
They're the kind of bastards who've done
every piece of trash work there is.

00:37:05.459 --> 00:37:07.862
I hired you to investigate
someone like that?

00:37:09.397 --> 00:37:10.531
You really don't remember, do you?

00:37:11.766 --> 00:37:13.935
His name is Lee Jong Su.
Forty-two years old.

00:37:13.935 --> 00:37:15.236
Single and unemployed.

00:37:15.236 --> 00:37:16.871
A hopeless,
bottom-of-the-barrel piece of garbage.

00:37:17.738 --> 00:37:19.006
But what's strange about him is,

00:37:19.006 --> 00:37:21.075
he used to have a perfectly decent job,

00:37:21.409 --> 00:37:22.777
then quit it overnight...

00:37:22.777 --> 00:37:24.779
and started running with thugs.

00:37:25.846 --> 00:37:28.783
The chauffeur
of the chairman of Mono Group...

00:37:28.783 --> 00:37:29.750
isn't some ordinary job.

00:37:30.251 --> 00:37:31.285
Mono Group?

00:37:31.285 --> 00:37:32.220
Yeah.

00:37:32.453 --> 00:37:35.856
Anyway, you asked me
for every bit of information on him.

00:37:35.856 --> 00:37:39.026
Personal details, relationships,
even where he lived.

00:37:42.430 --> 00:37:43.598
This is it.

00:37:43.598 --> 00:37:44.498
Thanks.

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:47.435
Not long after I started working the case,

00:37:47.435 --> 00:37:49.470
I'd already figured out everything else.

00:37:49.470 --> 00:37:51.172
But I just couldn't pin down
where he was living.

00:37:51.672 --> 00:37:52.907
But where could he really go?

00:37:53.507 --> 00:37:55.576
It took some doing, but not long after,

00:37:55.576 --> 00:37:57.245
I picked up his trail
through a crypto exchange.

00:38:00.381 --> 00:38:01.782
It's gone up a lot.

00:38:01.782 --> 00:38:02.717
Thank you.

00:38:03.718 --> 00:38:04.652
You're leaving already?

00:38:04.952 --> 00:38:06.520
At first,
I thought maybe I'd seen it wrong.

00:38:06.954 --> 00:38:08.556
I figured he'd struck it big somewhere,

00:38:08.556 --> 00:38:10.157
because his whole look
had suddenly changed.

00:38:10.491 --> 00:38:12.393
In that short amount of time,
he became a completely different person.

00:38:13.160 --> 00:38:15.897
So I contacted you right away,

00:38:17.098 --> 00:38:18.132
but your accident happened.

00:38:18.633 --> 00:38:19.901
I was in a dilemma too.

00:38:20.201 --> 00:38:22.270
My client was in the hospital
hovering between life and death,

00:38:22.270 --> 00:38:24.238
but my conscience wouldn't let me drop it.

00:38:26.107 --> 00:38:28.242
Why did I want this man investigated?

00:38:28.543 --> 00:38:29.644
You forgot that too?

00:38:30.011 --> 00:38:31.412
You mentioned blackmail.

00:38:31.612 --> 00:38:33.247
Someone was blackmailing me?

00:38:33.247 --> 00:38:34.181
No.

00:38:34.515 --> 00:38:35.449
Blackmailing your friend, Ms. Ham.

00:38:36.784 --> 00:38:38.386
Your symptoms are really serious.

00:38:39.020 --> 00:38:40.821
How can every answer be wrong?

00:38:41.422 --> 00:38:43.491
What kind of blackmail
was this man using...

00:38:43.491 --> 00:38:45.026
that I even hired someone to look into it?

00:38:45.259 --> 00:38:48.930
You said he even went to the studio
where she painted and harassed her,

00:38:49.196 --> 00:38:51.432
and that it seemed strange...

00:38:51.432 --> 00:38:52.466
watching her just take it.

00:38:52.633 --> 00:38:54.268
When you tried to help her,

00:38:54.268 --> 00:38:56.070
you said your friend stopped you.

00:38:56.404 --> 00:38:57.805
Your friend's name was...

00:38:57.805 --> 00:38:59.540
Hee Su? Hee...

00:38:59.540 --> 00:39:00.508
Choi Hee Su!

00:39:00.508 --> 00:39:03.277
Why did I say I wanted to meet
the man blackmailing Hee Su?

00:39:04.245 --> 00:39:06.647
And why did Hee Su
stop me from helping her?

00:39:07.315 --> 00:39:09.917
Whether we go forward with it now or not,

00:39:10.318 --> 00:39:11.719
that's for you to decide, Ms. Ham.

00:39:11.719 --> 00:39:14.355
I didn't get to finish the job,
but you still owe me the balance.

00:39:14.355 --> 00:39:16.691
It took a lot of work to dig up this much.

00:39:19.894 --> 00:39:21.295
Start again, please.

00:39:21.295 --> 00:39:22.463
I'll text you my account number.

00:39:22.463 --> 00:39:23.497
Don't forget this.

00:39:23.497 --> 00:39:25.032
And there's hazard pay too.

00:39:25.032 --> 00:39:27.168
If I get physically hurt
or put in danger while investigating...

00:39:27.168 --> 00:39:28.369
I'll give you whatever you want.

00:39:29.003 --> 00:39:30.371
But you have to find out...

00:39:30.872 --> 00:39:33.808
where this Lee Jong Su is
and what he's doing now.

00:39:33.808 --> 00:39:35.142
Please make sure I get to meet him.

00:39:35.142 --> 00:39:36.911
Okay, deal!

00:39:36.911 --> 00:39:39.247
First, finding that bastard Lee Jong Su...

00:39:39.247 --> 00:39:40.281
is the key to this whole thing.

00:39:40.648 --> 00:39:42.884
By the way, is there anything
you want to ask me for?

00:39:42.884 --> 00:39:44.752
Say the word.
I'll throw it in as a freebie.

00:39:48.723 --> 00:39:49.891
Restore it, please.

00:39:50.157 --> 00:39:51.325
As fast as you can.

00:39:52.693 --> 00:39:54.495
This house is amazing.

00:39:54.495 --> 00:39:56.130
Even the slippers are cute.

00:39:57.398 --> 00:39:59.533
Myo Jin.

00:40:01.535 --> 00:40:03.104
I've missed you.

00:40:03.571 --> 00:40:04.805
It must've been hard.

00:40:05.072 --> 00:40:06.207
You went through a lot.

00:40:06.207 --> 00:40:07.909
Goodness,
look how thin your face has gotten.

00:40:08.376 --> 00:40:10.578
Have you been eating properly?

00:40:13.247 --> 00:40:14.982
We all know each other well.

00:40:14.982 --> 00:40:16.050
She's a good friend.

00:40:16.517 --> 00:40:19.820
She'll probably take
better care of you than I do.

00:40:20.555 --> 00:40:22.590
She's going to stay here with us
for a while.

00:40:23.090 --> 00:40:24.091
That's okay, right?

00:40:26.460 --> 00:40:29.230
Where was it that we met?

00:40:29.497 --> 00:40:30.398
What?

00:40:30.398 --> 00:40:31.766
You don't recognize me?

00:40:32.133 --> 00:40:33.901
You don't remember? I'm Ri A.

00:40:33.901 --> 00:40:35.703
You always said my name was pretty.

00:40:36.871 --> 00:40:38.439
We all traveled together,

00:40:38.439 --> 00:40:39.974
and we went hiking several times too.

00:40:40.708 --> 00:40:42.143
I see.

00:40:44.512 --> 00:40:46.347
No way, that ring.

00:40:47.348 --> 00:40:49.116
Did he propose?

00:40:49.116 --> 00:40:51.819
That's incredible.

00:40:52.587 --> 00:40:54.689
Ryu Jun Ho is famous...

00:40:54.689 --> 00:40:56.390
for being insanely picky about women.

00:40:56.390 --> 00:40:57.592
There she goes again.

00:40:57.758 --> 00:40:58.960
It's true.

00:40:58.960 --> 00:41:01.796
News anchors, models, business heiresses.

00:41:01.796 --> 00:41:03.297
Every woman who thought
she had a shot took one,

00:41:03.297 --> 00:41:05.266
and he turned every single one down.

00:41:05.266 --> 00:41:07.668
If people heard you,
they'd think it was all true.

00:41:07.668 --> 00:41:08.970
It is true, though.

00:41:11.505 --> 00:41:14.008
I'll head upstairs first.

00:41:14.342 --> 00:41:15.643
Okay.

00:41:15.643 --> 00:41:16.611
Go on up and rest.

00:41:28.956 --> 00:41:31.392
Isn't she worse off
than what you told me...

00:41:31.392 --> 00:41:32.293
if she's at that level?

00:41:32.293 --> 00:41:33.995
That's why I'm saying it's dangerous.

00:41:34.996 --> 00:41:36.664
You need to stay by her side
and watch her.

00:41:37.899 --> 00:41:40.534
Don't worry about anything else.
Just keep your promise.

00:41:50.378 --> 00:41:53.447
How long are they going
to keep living like this?

00:42:05.993 --> 00:42:07.361
Aren't you bored?

00:42:08.095 --> 00:42:11.065
I heard that ever since you got into
that accident when you went biking alone,

00:42:11.065 --> 00:42:12.567
you've basically been stuck at home.

00:42:13.668 --> 00:42:15.136
Right.

00:42:15.636 --> 00:42:17.538
I was being stubborn
and didn't listen to Jun Ho.

00:42:17.538 --> 00:42:19.207
Jun Ho had work,

00:42:19.207 --> 00:42:21.008
so he headed to the site
a little while ago.

00:42:21.008 --> 00:42:23.644
He asked me to make sure
you wouldn't get bored,

00:42:24.946 --> 00:42:26.547
and that just so happens
to be my specialty.

00:42:28.249 --> 00:42:29.584
No, it's okay.

00:42:29.784 --> 00:42:31.519
Please just go do your own thing, Ri A.

00:42:31.519 --> 00:42:32.987
Let's see.

00:42:32.987 --> 00:42:34.121
There it is.

00:42:35.856 --> 00:42:36.724
The car key.

00:42:37.191 --> 00:42:38.993
- Let's go.
- What?

00:42:39.694 --> 00:42:40.661
Go where?

00:42:40.895 --> 00:42:41.996
Just come with me.

00:42:42.530 --> 00:42:44.599
It's not somewhere
Jun Ho would be thrilled to hear about.

00:42:45.366 --> 00:42:46.300
Wait.

00:42:47.034 --> 00:42:48.402
If it's a place like that,
I don't want to go.

00:42:50.371 --> 00:42:52.206
You really have changed.

00:42:53.040 --> 00:42:53.774
What?

00:42:54.342 --> 00:42:56.644
Weren't you always the type
to act first and think later?

00:42:57.511 --> 00:42:59.347
I learned that
from watching you, you know.

00:43:10.324 --> 00:43:11.792
This is your car, Myo Jin.

00:43:11.792 --> 00:43:13.060
Do you want to try driving it yourself?

00:43:14.328 --> 00:43:16.364
That car is mine?

00:43:16.597 --> 00:43:17.632
Yes.

00:43:17.632 --> 00:43:19.100
Your old car...

00:43:19.100 --> 00:43:20.801
was totaled in the accident,

00:43:21.335 --> 00:43:23.571
and this one was something
Jun Ho bought for you as a discharge gift.

00:43:25.740 --> 00:43:27.975
I don't think I was very good at driving.

00:43:28.543 --> 00:43:30.344
You were basically a pro.

00:43:30.645 --> 00:43:32.547
I guess the accident
shook your confidence.

00:43:33.915 --> 00:43:35.149
Do you want to give it a try today?

00:43:36.217 --> 00:43:37.084
No.

00:43:39.053 --> 00:43:41.355
Okay. Then I'll drive today.

00:43:41.956 --> 00:43:42.790
Get in.

00:43:53.668 --> 00:43:55.903
Damn, this car is incredible.

00:43:56.237 --> 00:43:57.572
You're lucky, Myo Jin.

00:43:57.572 --> 00:43:59.607
What? Why?

00:43:59.607 --> 00:44:01.209
Your boyfriend's unreal.

00:44:01.642 --> 00:44:04.178
He's handsome, capable,
and makes crazy money.

00:44:04.612 --> 00:44:06.180
And on top of that,
he only has eyes for you.

00:44:06.581 --> 00:44:07.982
That's insane.

00:44:28.035 --> 00:44:28.869
Is that her?

00:44:29.804 --> 00:44:30.705
She's pretty.

00:44:31.005 --> 00:44:33.241
What's the point?
She's messed up in the head.

00:44:33.875 --> 00:44:35.109
That makes it better for us.

00:44:36.711 --> 00:44:38.112
What do you think
after seeing the estimate?

00:44:38.112 --> 00:44:39.080
Do you think the numbers look good?

00:44:40.348 --> 00:44:42.350
Let's each take one clean cut.

00:44:42.617 --> 00:44:44.719
I think that much
could come out pretty easy.

00:44:45.186 --> 00:44:46.053
You mean 100,000 dollars?

00:44:48.222 --> 00:44:49.624
Are we finally wiping out the debt?

00:44:50.391 --> 00:44:51.325
If this goes well.

00:44:51.759 --> 00:44:53.561
Hey, then let's squeeze
a little more while we're at it.

00:44:53.794 --> 00:44:55.096
It's not like chances like this
come around often.

00:44:55.096 --> 00:44:57.665
Things always fall apart
when you overdo it like that.

00:44:58.132 --> 00:44:59.634
Do you think
Ryu Jun Ho is some ordinary guy?

00:44:59.867 --> 00:45:01.168
Do you think connections are a joke?

00:45:03.037 --> 00:45:03.938
You're right.

00:45:07.608 --> 00:45:10.278
She goes to the hospital
or on simple errands by herself.

00:45:10.678 --> 00:45:13.414
She went out alone today too
and came back in the evening.

00:45:14.081 --> 00:45:15.349
Ryu Jun Ho's so busy...

00:45:15.349 --> 00:45:17.518
he doesn't seem to think much of that.

00:45:19.720 --> 00:45:20.855
That's our chance.

00:45:21.489 --> 00:45:23.224
I could do it right now.

00:45:23.224 --> 00:45:24.258
Are you kidding me?

00:45:24.525 --> 00:45:26.594
If that psycho gets kidnapped
the second I show up,

00:45:26.594 --> 00:45:28.162
who do you think
the police will suspect first?

00:45:29.664 --> 00:45:30.798
Do you think it'll take a while?

00:45:32.700 --> 00:45:33.601
No.

00:45:33.901 --> 00:45:35.736
Her mind's all over the place,

00:45:35.736 --> 00:45:36.938
so there should be plenty of chances.

00:46:04.232 --> 00:46:05.533
Hey, Ham Myo Jin.

00:46:06.167 --> 00:46:08.603
Why are you drinking alone? That's no fun.

00:46:09.370 --> 00:46:10.805
I'm fine.

00:46:11.372 --> 00:46:12.273
No, you're not.

00:46:13.641 --> 00:46:14.442
Let's go.

00:46:15.209 --> 00:46:16.944
Come on, hurry.

00:46:17.278 --> 00:46:18.746
- Come on.
- I said I'm fine.

00:46:22.550 --> 00:46:23.384
Come on.

00:47:28.616 --> 00:47:29.450
Hee Su!

00:47:44.098 --> 00:47:44.999
Darn it.

00:47:49.036 --> 00:47:50.104
Move.

00:47:50.104 --> 00:47:51.472
Move!

00:47:53.708 --> 00:47:55.877
My face.

00:47:55.877 --> 00:47:57.078
Look at you.

00:47:57.078 --> 00:47:59.780
Hey, I'm hurting just watching that.

00:48:01.415 --> 00:48:02.683
You little...

00:48:12.560 --> 00:48:13.394
What the...

00:48:14.128 --> 00:48:15.396
What's with her?

00:48:34.181 --> 00:48:35.650
You're dead today.

00:48:39.754 --> 00:48:41.322
That startled me.

00:48:41.322 --> 00:48:42.256
Hee Su.

00:48:42.957 --> 00:48:44.759
Do you want to join in too?

00:48:46.060 --> 00:48:47.361
That works for me.

00:48:53.067 --> 00:48:53.935
What?

00:48:56.470 --> 00:48:57.305
Shit.

00:48:57.972 --> 00:48:59.040
Are you insane?

00:48:59.473 --> 00:49:01.042
You need to bleed too.

00:49:09.483 --> 00:49:10.384
Hee Su.

00:49:10.384 --> 00:49:11.352
Get up.

00:49:12.920 --> 00:49:13.788
Choi Hee Su.

00:49:17.158 --> 00:49:18.092
Myo Jin.

00:49:25.499 --> 00:49:27.501
Get that away from me.

00:49:34.675 --> 00:49:35.443
Get up.

00:49:40.314 --> 00:49:41.148
What happened?

00:49:41.148 --> 00:49:42.783
My goodness. Blood.

00:49:43.417 --> 00:49:44.318
She's bleeding.

00:49:44.318 --> 00:49:45.586
- Isn't that blood?
- She's bleeding.

00:49:57.365 --> 00:49:58.199
Are you okay?

00:49:59.400 --> 00:50:00.368
It hurts so bad.

00:50:03.738 --> 00:50:04.639
Ham Myo Jin.

00:50:06.173 --> 00:50:07.241
Are you serious?

00:50:08.209 --> 00:50:09.777
Where does that kind of guts come from?

00:50:12.113 --> 00:50:13.381
When I get mad,

00:50:14.315 --> 00:50:15.550
I sometimes lose it.

00:50:17.151 --> 00:50:18.986
But still,

00:50:19.287 --> 00:50:20.755
weren't you scared back there?

00:50:21.022 --> 00:50:22.990
Scared? Please.

00:50:22.990 --> 00:50:24.292
You were in that state.

00:50:24.292 --> 00:50:26.027
I had to fight
like my life depended on it.

00:50:28.763 --> 00:50:31.399
Damn those bastards.

00:50:31.766 --> 00:50:33.100
I thought I was going to die.

00:50:34.869 --> 00:50:36.404
Why did you do that back there?

00:50:37.271 --> 00:50:39.006
Did you think I was going to stab you?

00:50:39.240 --> 00:50:40.174
It's just,

00:50:40.741 --> 00:50:42.176
I can't handle sharp things.

00:50:42.510 --> 00:50:43.477
What?

00:50:44.111 --> 00:50:45.179
It's hereditary.

00:50:45.680 --> 00:50:46.981
My dad's exactly the same.

00:50:48.349 --> 00:50:50.251
You're just like a little kid.

00:50:51.152 --> 00:50:52.853
Do I have to keep
protecting you like this?

00:51:01.862 --> 00:51:02.763
Why?

00:51:03.130 --> 00:51:04.232
Why do you look like that?

00:51:04.865 --> 00:51:05.800
I'm mad.

00:51:07.368 --> 00:51:09.637
Even if we report them to the police,

00:51:09.637 --> 00:51:11.239
they'll be out again in no time.

00:51:11.806 --> 00:51:12.807
Don't worry.

00:51:14.408 --> 00:51:16.210
I already told my dad everything.

00:51:18.379 --> 00:51:20.414
Didn't you say he was overseas right now?

00:51:21.115 --> 00:51:23.017
I didn't tell him to come back.

00:51:23.017 --> 00:51:25.019
I told him to send people
and get it handled.

00:51:27.521 --> 00:51:29.023
You made him worried.

00:51:30.191 --> 00:51:31.592
Did he say when he was coming back?

00:51:33.427 --> 00:51:36.764
There are people everywhere
trying to squeeze money out of him,

00:51:38.432 --> 00:51:41.202
and that's why he tries
not to come back much.

00:51:42.803 --> 00:51:44.005
My dad...

00:51:44.805 --> 00:51:47.642
is some self-made chairman
of a major corporation for everyone else.

00:51:49.977 --> 00:51:51.178
But to me,

00:51:51.846 --> 00:51:53.781
he's just an ordinary old man...

00:51:53.781 --> 00:51:55.182
who's already well past
the twilight of his life,

00:51:58.052 --> 00:51:59.954
and who'll spend the rest of it...

00:51:59.954 --> 00:52:01.822
suffering because he has
a delinquent daughter like me.

00:52:13.935 --> 00:52:16.437
(Powerful business family's villa
explosion caused by gas leak)

00:52:16.437 --> 00:52:18.105
(Chairman Choi Young Ho of Mono Group...)

00:52:18.105 --> 00:52:19.774
(and his only blood relative,
Ms. Choi, have died.)

00:52:25.146 --> 00:52:26.747
(Mono Group Chairman Choi Young Ho...)

00:52:26.747 --> 00:52:28.216
(and Ms. Choi were found dead
in the blast.)

00:52:28.216 --> 00:52:30.952
(Police said they are also leaving open
the possibility of arson.)

00:52:38.659 --> 00:52:40.761
(Hanguk Somang Hospital)

00:52:48.569 --> 00:52:49.437
Thank you.

00:52:56.410 --> 00:52:57.511
It's unusual.

00:52:58.312 --> 00:53:01.482
Honestly, I prefer tea to coffee.

00:53:01.716 --> 00:53:03.618
I don't recommend coffee either.

00:53:04.318 --> 00:53:07.355
The effects of caffeine
don't really suit my work.

00:53:07.622 --> 00:53:08.623
You're truly...

00:53:09.490 --> 00:53:10.591
very meticulous.

00:53:12.026 --> 00:53:14.362
That's probably why...

00:53:15.429 --> 00:53:17.298
I've always trusted you, Dr. Jung.

00:53:18.866 --> 00:53:20.134
Actually,

00:53:20.501 --> 00:53:21.569
has Myo Jin...

00:53:23.337 --> 00:53:27.008
ever mentioned a friend named Choi Hee Su?

00:53:27.508 --> 00:53:28.409
No.

00:53:28.676 --> 00:53:30.478
That's the first time
I've heard that name.

00:53:31.879 --> 00:53:34.382
I see. She said she learned about her...

00:53:34.382 --> 00:53:37.385
from a friend she ran into by chance
at the hospital.

00:53:38.819 --> 00:53:42.523
Maybe she just hasn't
mentioned it to you yet.

00:53:42.790 --> 00:53:44.692
She seemed very curious about her with me.

00:53:45.226 --> 00:53:46.928
Do you know her?

00:53:47.595 --> 00:53:49.130
Then I suppose she'd ask.

00:53:49.363 --> 00:53:52.533
I only told her what little I remembered.

00:53:52.533 --> 00:53:55.069
She wasn't that important a friend.

00:53:59.373 --> 00:54:01.008
This may be an improper question,

00:54:02.009 --> 00:54:03.544
but during treatment,

00:54:04.278 --> 00:54:06.080
is it possible for a patient to lie?

00:54:06.781 --> 00:54:09.917
If someone's in a situation
where the line between real memory...

00:54:11.385 --> 00:54:13.020
and illusion is blurred,

00:54:13.020 --> 00:54:15.423
I thought it could definitely happen.

00:54:15.623 --> 00:54:17.058
It's not impossible,

00:54:17.058 --> 00:54:18.926
but it's not something
that can be judged lightly.

00:54:19.894 --> 00:54:22.230
Calling what a patient says a lie...

00:54:22.230 --> 00:54:24.999
is a one-sided view
held by the person listening.

00:54:26.901 --> 00:54:28.369
Then what if the patient...

00:54:28.369 --> 00:54:30.905
knows that they're lying?

00:54:31.372 --> 00:54:32.940
Isn't that...

00:54:34.008 --> 00:54:35.176
a different matter?

00:54:35.576 --> 00:54:37.678
Unless the patient says so directly,

00:54:38.946 --> 00:54:41.816
that, too, isn't something
we can judge carelessly.

00:54:42.450 --> 00:54:43.317
Doctor.

00:54:44.552 --> 00:54:46.053
Are my questions...

00:54:49.657 --> 00:54:50.791
making you uncomfortable?

00:54:51.392 --> 00:54:52.293
Pardon?

00:54:52.293 --> 00:54:54.762
Coming here out of the blue...

00:54:54.762 --> 00:54:56.964
to ask about a friend
who doesn't even seem that important,

00:54:58.199 --> 00:55:00.635
and asking if the patient might be lying.

00:55:01.736 --> 00:55:02.870
Even I can see...

00:55:04.038 --> 00:55:06.507
how that could catch you off guard.

00:55:08.242 --> 00:55:09.644
This isn't a normal situation.

00:55:11.779 --> 00:55:13.714
I've been struggling with it.

00:55:14.448 --> 00:55:16.851
But this isn't something
I can just let slide,

00:55:16.851 --> 00:55:18.853
so I'm asking you directly.

00:55:19.420 --> 00:55:20.454
Myo Jin...

00:55:22.623 --> 00:55:24.559
is acting out of character.

00:55:25.626 --> 00:55:28.029
I don't believe
it's anything to be concerned about.

00:55:28.963 --> 00:55:30.731
A patient's words and actions...

00:55:31.332 --> 00:55:33.568
can appear irregular and contradictory.

00:55:39.874 --> 00:55:42.610
Trusting and waiting
isn't as easy as it sounds.

00:55:43.811 --> 00:55:45.346
It can be tedious and frustrating.

00:55:46.681 --> 00:55:49.850
Especially for a guardian
who wants the patient to recover...

00:55:49.850 --> 00:55:51.419
as soon as possible.

00:55:55.323 --> 00:55:56.591
Really?

00:56:04.298 --> 00:56:06.067
Then I suppose...

00:56:06.434 --> 00:56:07.635
there are only two possibilities.

00:56:10.671 --> 00:56:13.040
Either I'm not qualified
to be her guardian,

00:56:14.942 --> 00:56:15.943
or you, Dr. Jung,

00:56:19.914 --> 00:56:21.315
are lying.

00:57:05.476 --> 00:57:10.228
(REVERSE)

00:57:10.598 --> 00:57:12.633
Why haven't you told me until now...

00:57:12.633 --> 00:57:13.868
about Hee Su
and your relationship, Jun Ho?

00:57:14.168 --> 00:57:15.269
Why did you do that?

00:57:15.269 --> 00:57:16.571
You didn't forget, did you?

00:57:16.837 --> 00:57:20.141
I'm not giving you this gift for nothing.

00:57:20.441 --> 00:57:22.877
I'm out of patience now.

00:57:22.877 --> 00:57:25.046
I don't even know what I'll do.

00:57:25.046 --> 00:57:25.913
You bastard.

00:57:26.480 --> 00:57:28.282
If both of them are avoiding me,

00:57:28.282 --> 00:57:29.917
then I must be involved somehow.

00:57:30.218 --> 00:57:32.086
How reckless of you to come here.

00:57:32.420 --> 00:57:34.355
By the time you realize it,
it'll already be too late.

00:57:34.822 --> 00:57:36.691
So watch yourself.

00:57:38.406 --> 00:57:40.406
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)